{"seq":1,"slug":"architectural-history","title":"建筑历史与理论","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/architectural-history","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"western-architecture-overview","title":"大学建筑学 — 西方建筑史概览","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/architectural-history/western-architecture-overview","wordCount":1553,"readingTime":7},{"seq":2,"slug":"chinese-timber-architecture","title":"大学建筑学 — 中国木构建筑体系","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/architectural-history/chinese-timber-architecture","wordCount":1445,"readingTime":6},{"seq":3,"slug":"modernism-and-beyond","title":"大学建筑学 — 现代主义及其之后","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/engineering/architecture/architectural-history/modernism-and-beyond","wordCount":1484,"readingTime":6}],"introMarkdown":"# 建筑历史与理论\n\n建筑历史不是一串风格名词的罗列，而是一部\"约束与突破\"的连续剧：每一种新风格的诞生，几乎都源于一种新材料、新结构或新社会需求打破了旧的限制。理解了拱券为什么取代了梁柱、钢与混凝土为什么催生了现代主义，你就握住了读懂任何建筑的钥匙。\n\n本章分三课。第一课纵览西方建筑从古希腊到现代的主线，第二课走进中国木构建筑这一独立而成熟的体系，第三课聚焦二十世纪的现代主义革命及其后的多元探索。三课合起来，为你建立一个跨越东西方、贯通古今的历史坐标系。\n"}